=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r1
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** FRR routing daemon stack on the edge router r1.

**Mechanism:** r1's FRR configuration includes `default-information originate` under `router ospf`, which causes r1 to inject a default route (0.0.0.0/0) into the OSPF domain whenever its own default gateway (203.0.113.1 via ispa on eth2) is reachable. With FRR inactive, no OSPF process runs, no adjacencies form with csw1 or csw2, and no default route is ever advertised into the campus fabric. Every core and distribution switch therefore has a full internal topology table (29 OSPF routes covering all office subnets) but zero entry for 0.0.0.0/0. Internet-bound traffic from any office host reaches csw1 or csw2, finds no matching route, and is silently dropped.

**Localization:** r1 — `systemctl is-active frr` returns `inactive`; `pgrep ospfd` returns nothing; csw1's full RIB confirms the absence of any default route. r1's own kernel table retains the static default via 203.0.113.1, so r1 itself can reach the internet — only the internal fabric is blind to it.

**Root cause:** The FRR service on r1 was not started (or crashed and was not restarted), silencing the OSPF default-route origination that the entire campus depends on for internet access.

**Fix:** Run `systemctl start frr` on r1. Once FRR comes up, ospfd will establish adjacencies with csw1 and csw2 and immediately redistribute the default route via `default-information originate`, restoring internet connectivity to all office hosts.
=== END ===